# Cursor Rules — KarstResConverter

## Project

C++17 CMake map/GIS data processing tool with ImGui + DirectX 11 GUI.

## Skills

This project includes two agent skills libraries that you MUST use:

### Development Workflow (superpowers-main/skills/)
Read the SKILL.md in each folder when the trigger matches:

- `brainstorming/` — Before any feature work or creative task
- `writing-plans/` — When creating implementation plans
- `executing-plans/` — When implementing from a plan
- `test-driven-development/` — Before writing implementation code
- `systematic-debugging/` — When encountering bugs or unexpected behavior
- `verification-before-completion/` — Before declaring work done
- `subagent-driven-development/` — For parallel task dispatch
- `requesting-code-review/` — After completing implementation
- `receiving-code-review/` — When responding to review feedback
- `dispatching-parallel-agents/` — For concurrent agent workflows
- `using-git-worktrees/` — For parallel development branches
- `finishing-a-development-branch/` — Merge/PR decisions
- `writing-skills/` — Creating new skills

### Context Engineering (Agent-Skills-for-Context-Engineering-main/skills/)
Read the SKILL.md in each folder when building AI agent systems:

- `context-fundamentals/` — Context windows and attention mechanics
- `context-degradation/` — Diagnosing context failures
- `context-compression/` — Reducing token usage
- `context-optimization/` — KV-cache, compaction, masking
- `multi-agent-patterns/` — Supervisor, swarm, hierarchical patterns
- `memory-systems/` — Agent memory and knowledge graphs
- `tool-design/` — Building effective agent tools
- `filesystem-context/` — File-based context management
- `hosted-agents/` — Background agent infrastructure
- `evaluation/` — Agent evaluation frameworks
- `advanced-evaluation/` — LLM-as-judge techniques
- `project-development/` — LLM project methodology
- `bdi-mental-states/` — BDI cognitive architecture

## Coding Rules

- C++17 standard, CMake 3.10+
- Follow existing ImGui patterns in WindowTool.cpp
- Use std::filesystem for path handling
- Use nlohmann::json for JSON
- Chinese comments are fine
- RAII for DirectX resources
- Save design docs to docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md
